<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, soymeal prices steady, oil falls.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, soymeal prices steady, oil falls.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady on Thursday in limited trading, dealers said. Most of the markets were closed due for 'Amavasya.'</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was down by 200 rupees per tonne and soyoil refined was down by 100 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady. Soymeal yellow was $295-296 September-October shipment of current season. For new season soymeal yellow was $280 per tonne November, December and January shipment.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $130 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,500 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,450 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
